"No," Leila writes, glowing azure letters hanging in the air beside her shoulder. "He carried no equipment during our flight from Thilias, so I have no transceiver channel. He promised he would establish contact once I reached Ollendor, but finding us will take time."

"Our arrival will not remain quiet for long," Daren assures her with a faint smile. "Once the commotion begins, he will know where to look."

"Let us hope so," Leila writes.

The surrounding architecture grows stranger with every block. Tall, cylindrical towers with curved glass facades stand alongside four-story residential spires built entirely of riveted metal, their plates dusted with a shimmering coating of seredium. No two structures share a blueprint; the entire district looks like an assortment of competing prototypes thrown together without a master plan.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch02b-Weird, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02b-Weird)


ID: B3-Ch02a-Insane
TEXT:

#if(v_b3_ch2_infiltration == 0 || v_b3_ch2_infiltration == 2) {
 "Reached him on the transceiver," I say. "The phrase is 'gargoyle wings.'"

The sentry's eyes narrow into cold slits. "Gargoyle wings? You certain of that?"

"Quite certain," I say.

"Right," the sentry says, stepping back toward the guardhouse door. "You are under arrest. You sit in the cells until this patron comes forward to vouch for you. If no one appears within a month, you hang for attempted infiltration."

"What?" I say, stepping forward. "We gave you the words!"

"You gave half the passphrase," the sentry snaps, resting a hand on his hilt. "The phrase requires a counter-sign gesture to foil eavesdroppers. You are in breach of city law. Step forward and surrender your steel. Do not make this bloody."

The sentry turns to lead us toward the guardhouse. Hadrik glances at Daren, who answers with a tight, grim nod.

"Hold on," Daren says, stepping forward and planting a heavy, steel-clad gauntlet onto the sentry's shoulder. "You overlooked one detail."

"Oh?" The man turns, frowning. "What detail?"

Before the sentry can draw breath, Hadrik bolts past him, closing the distance to the iron automata stationed before the portal.

The dwarf launches into the air, driving a massive, aura-hardened fist straight into the first golem's visor. The iron faceplate caves inward with a deafening screech of buckled steel, and the construct hurtles backward through the air, slamming into the gates. The iron doors tear from their hinges in a spray of stone dust and sheared bolts. The fallen golem thrashes in the wreckage, trying to find footing, but Hadrik drops onto its chest and hammers a brutal flurry of punches into the core housing until the metal cracks, sparks flare, and the frame goes cold.

"Are you insane?" the sentry yells, reaching for his hilt.

Daren brings the rim of his heavy heater shield around in a sharp arc, striking the guard across the temple. The man drops like a sack of grain into the dirt.

"Into the barrier!" Daren roars.

He raises his shield, and a shimmering, translucent dome of white force locks into place around us. Further out along the perimeter ditch, four more iron automata turn their massive visors toward our position, heat radiating from their chest vents as their jaws unhinge to charge simultaneous flame beams.

"Brace," Daren grunts. "Heat incoming."

}
#if(v_b3_ch2_infiltration == 1) {
 "Not quite," I say as Hadrik bolts past the guard, lunging toward the iron automata before the gate.

The dwarf launches into the air, driving a massive, aura-hardened fist straight into the first golem's visor. The iron faceplate caves inward with a deafening screech of buckled steel, and the construct hurtles backward through the air, slamming into the gates. The iron doors tear from their hinges in a spray of stone dust and sheared bolts. The fallen golem thrashes in the wreckage, trying to find footing, but Hadrik drops onto its chest and hammers a brutal flurry of punches into the core housing until the metal cracks, sparks flare, and the frame goes cold.

"Are you insane?" the sentry yells, reaching for his hilt.

Daren brings the rim of his heavy heater shield around in a sharp arc, striking the guard across the temple. The man drops like a sack of grain into the dirt.

"Into the barrier!" Daren roars.

He raises his shield, and a shimmering, translucent dome of white force locks into place around us. Further out along the perimeter ditch, four more iron automata turn their massive visors toward our position, heat radiating from their chest vents as their jaws unhinge to charge simultaneous flame beams.

"Brace," Daren grunts. "Heat incoming."

}
choice("Continue", B3-Ch02a-Insane2, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02a-Insane2)


ID: B3-Ch02a-Insane2
TEXT:

 Four concentrated torrents of magical fire slam into Daren's barrier at once. The air inside the perimeter flashes blinding white, and the temperature spikes so violently my skin pricks with instant sweat. The constructs plant their heavy iron feet to channel the heat, locked in rigid firing stances. Across the ditch, Hadrik lunges at the second golem, but this one parries with a sweeping iron forearm, forcing the dwarf into a low roll to avoid being pinned against the crossfire.

"Kate, shatter one of them!" Daren shouts through gritted teeth, his boots sliding back through the gravel under the immense thermal pressure. "I cannot advance the ward under four continuous channels!"

"I am holding the parapet line!" Kate calls back.

Above us, dozens of ice platforms whip through the air, intercepting a relentless hail of crossbow bolts and iron-tipped arrows raining from the wall garrison.

"Drop those shields and the arrows shred us," Kate snaps, her voice strained. "Target the hulls yourselves!"

"Right!" Daren thrusts his enchanted blade through the front edge of the barrier. The steel glows cherry-red, drawing the raw fire from the nearest stream like water into a siphon. Once the blade reaches white heat, Daren brings it around with a roar, throwing a concentrated shockwave of compressed flame back down the path.

The fire wave collides with the golem's channel. The explosion tears the ground open, throwing the automaton onto its back and sending spiderweb fractures across the face of Daren's barrier.

"Flower and I take the parapet," Illuna says, her eyes flashing bright blue as she takes control of the shared body.

"Neutralize only!" Daren barks. "No slaughter!"

"Moving," Illuna says, vaulting clear of the ward. Flame jets erupt from Flower's feet, hurtling her straight up toward the parapets.

"Flight currents active, Barry," Melindra murmurs, and a tight coil of compressed air wraps around my torso. "Do not waste them."

choice("Fly into the air and help Illuna take out the guards on the walls", B3-Ch02a-Observation, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02a-Observation, v_b3_ch2_golems = 0)
choice("Fly out of the barrier and try to distract some of the golems", B3-Ch02a-Reflexes, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02a-Reflexes, v_b3_ch2_golems = 1)
choice("Make a run for it and try to distract the golems with my speed.", B3-Ch02a-Speed, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02a-Speed, v_b3_ch2_golems = 2)
choice("Fly out of the barrier and try to punch one of the golems in the face.", B3-Ch02a-Strength, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02a-Strength, v_b3_ch2_golems = 3)


ID: B3-Ch02a-Observation
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_perception < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_perception == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2)
#if(v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_perception < 4) {
 "I'll go help Illuna," I say. "Clear the archers first."

I unhitch my crossbow, thrust my arms upward to signal the air currents, and launch toward the wall parapet. A golem below tracks my ascent, snapping its jaws shut and retargeting its flame jet into the sky. I bank hard to slip the searing beam, but half a dozen archers along the stone walkway pivot and loose a dense spread of iron bolts in my path.

I weave frantically through the air currents to dodge the incoming iron. Above the battlements, Illuna releases a sweeping flood of pressurized water across the masonry, washing three crossbowmen off their feet and over the inner rail.

Before I can align my sight to fire, intense heat washes over my neck from behind. A second automaton has pivoted on the ditch, tracking my flight path. The fire beam hits me square between the shoulder blades, reducing flesh and gear to cinders before I can draw breath.

}
#if(v_perception == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
 "I'll go help Illuna," I say. "Clear the archers first."

I unhitch my crossbow, thrust my arms upward to signal the air currents, and launch toward the wall parapet. A golem below tracks my ascent, snapping its jaws shut and retargeting its flame jet into the sky. I bank hard to slip the searing beam, but half a dozen archers along the stone walkway pivot and loose a dense spread of iron bolts in my path.

I weave frantically through the air currents to dodge the incoming iron. Above the battlements, Illuna releases a sweeping flood of pressurized water across the masonry, washing three crossbowmen off their feet and over the inner rail.

A flicker of white light in my peripheral vision catches my eye—a second golem near the ditch unhinging its jaw, aiming directly at my back. I tuck into a sharp spiral, diving under the searing heat as the beam scorches the air inches above my head.

Rather than fleeing the crossfire, I level out and hover directly between the ditch golems and the parapet archers. The constructs immediately clamp their jaws shut, aborting their flame channels to avoid incinerating their own men on the battlements. Maintaining altitude, I strafe along the wall, snapping crossbow bolts into the legs and shoulders of the garrison archers to pin them to the stone. With their primary lane blocked, the two grounded golems pivot away to target Hadrik, who has already dismantled the gate sentry and is closing on the third construct.

With fewer beams battering the ward, Daren advances at a steady march, shielding Kate, Leila, and Melindra toward the breach. As Illuna and I clear the remaining archers, Kate dismisses her overhead ice shields and channels her magic into a massive, heavily compressed icicle floating above the ditch, honing its tip to pierce anti-magic hull plating.

With a sharp whip of her arm, Kate drives the giant frost lance downward. The projectile breaks the sound barrier with a concussive boom, punching through the golem's central hull plate and driving the machine into the dirt, dead and smoking. Nearby, Hadrik caves in the fourth golem's chest with a two-handed hammer blow.

Heavy stomping vibrates through the valley. A dozen more iron golems from the outer patrol rings are closing in fast, their chest vents glowing as they prepare to fire. Hadrik engages the closest, while the last active beam pivots toward Flower and Illuna in the sky.

Daren reaches the broken archway and yells back across the rubble.

"Fall back to the gate!" he roars. "Disengage and move! Before the second wave locks us down!"

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_perception < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_perception < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_perception < 4)
choice("Continue", B3-Ch02a-Rubble, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02a-Rubble) if (v_perception == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2)


ID: B3-Ch02a-Reflexes
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_reflexes < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_reflexes == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2)
#if(v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_reflexes < 4) {
 "I'll go distract some of the golems," I say. "Push for the gatehouse. I will regroup at the threshold."

I unhitch my crossbow, raise my arms to engage Melindra's air currents, and rocket toward the cluster of automata along the ditch. I keep well clear of the parapet line to avoid drawing the garrison archers, leaving the battlements to Illuna.

Once in range, I loose three bolts into the nearest golem hulls. The iron points ricochet harmlessly off the plating, but the clang serves its purpose. All three constructs break their channels on Daren's ward, turning their hollow visors toward the sky. Jaws drop, and three thick beams of white flame lash across the air.

I bank and dive in erratic spirals, but evading three converging heat beams in open air proves too much. My timing slips by a fraction of a second, and a crossfire beam clips my flank, vaporizing me instantly.

}
#if(v_reflexes == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
 "I'll go distract some of the golems," I say. "Push for the gatehouse. I will regroup at the threshold."

I unhitch my crossbow, raise my arms to engage Melindra's air currents, and rocket toward the cluster of automata along the ditch. I keep well clear of the parapet line to avoid drawing the garrison archers, leaving the battlements to Illuna.

Once in range, I loose three bolts into the nearest golem hulls. The iron points ricochet harmlessly off the plating, but the clang serves its purpose. All three constructs break their channels on Daren's ward, turning their hollow visors toward the sky. Jaws drop, and three thick beams of white flame lash across the air.

The searing beams weave a deadly grid across the sky, but enhanced reflexes keep my body moving a split second ahead of each pulse. I drop, roll, and accelerate through the gaps in the crossfire. Hadrik shatters the gate sentry and charges into the ditch, driving a fist into the nearest automaton and forcing it to abort its channel to parry his assault.

Glancing down, I see Daren's barrier moving swiftly toward the shattered gate. With Illuna dispersing the archers above, Kate pulls her magic from defense and compresses a massive frost lance in the sky, reinforcing its core against anti-magic wards.

Kate snaps her arm down. The massive frost lance punches through the sky with a sonic crack, piercing straight through the skull of the second golem on my flank and driving the wreckage deep into the gravel. Hadrik finishes his target a heartbeat later, tearing off its weapon arm.

Heavy stomping vibrates through the valley. A dozen more iron golems from the outer patrol rings are closing in fast, their chest vents glowing as they prepare to fire. Hadrik engages the closest, while the last active beam pivots toward Flower and Illuna in the sky.

Daren reaches the broken archway and yells back across the rubble.

"Fall back to the gate!" he roars. "Disengage and move! Before the second wave locks us down!"

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_reflexes < 4)
