ID: B3-Ch02a-Strength
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch2_metal,1) if (v_strength == 4 && v_toughness == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_toughness == 4 && v_strength < 4 || v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_toughness < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_strength == 4 && v_toughness == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2)
achievement("Metal golem slayer",v_ac_b3_ch2_metal)
#if(v_b3_ch1_unlock == 2 || v_toughness < 4) {
 "I'll try to deal with one of the golems," I say. "The quicker we take them out, the better."

"You plan to engage an automaton bare-handed?" Daren shouts. "Barry, that is sui—"

I cut him off, throwing my arms up to signal Melindra's currents, and launch into the upper air currents above the crossfire. Scanning the ditch, I pick out the most isolated of the four constructs targeting Daren's ward.

I dive vertically, thrusting both fists forward to maximize the dive speed. Closing within striking distance, I put my entire weight into a crushing punch directly into the golem's iron visor.

My knuckles strike solid, unyielding iron. Bone shatters in my hand, the shock reverberating up my forearm like a hammer blow against an anvil. The golem barely flinches. Agony blinds me as I try to reverse the currents, but the construct's jaws unhinge, and a point-blank blast of white fire reduces me to ashes.

}
#if(v_toughness == 4 && v_strength < 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
 "I'll try to deal with one of the golems," I say. "The quicker we take them out, the better."

"You plan to engage an automaton bare-handed?" Daren shouts. "Barry, that is sui—"

I cut him off, throwing my arms up to signal Melindra's currents, and launch into the upper air currents above the crossfire. Scanning the ditch, I pick out the most isolated of the four constructs targeting Daren's ward.

I dive vertically, thrusting both fists forward to maximize the dive speed. Closing within striking distance, I put my entire weight into a crushing punch directly into the golem's iron visor.

My reinforced frame absorbs the shock of impact, but my raw striking power fails to buckle the hull. The golem absorbs the momentum without yielding an inch. I reverse currents to clear the blast radius, but the machine pivots instantly, releasing a point-blank torrent of flame that incinerates me on the spot.

}
#if(v_strength == 4 && v_toughness == 4 && v_b3_ch1_unlock != 2) {
 "I'll try to deal with one of the golems," I say. "The quicker we take them out, the better."

"You plan to engage an automaton bare-handed?" Daren shouts. "Barry, that is sui—"

I cut him off, throwing my arms up to signal Melindra's currents, and launch into the upper air currents above the crossfire. Scanning the ditch, I pick out the most isolated of the four constructs targeting Daren's ward.

I dive vertically, thrusting both fists forward to maximize the dive speed. Closing within striking distance, I put my entire weight into a crushing punch directly into the golem's iron visor.

The concussive strike buckles the faceplate with a deafening screech, throwing the heavy construct onto its back. Pain shoots through my knuckles, and pneumatic strain tears at the tendons of my shoulder, but the reinforced bone holds firm. I draw my dagger mid-drop, landing on the golem's chest and driving the hardened steel into its left optic sensor. The machine thrashes violently, internal gears grinding as it tries to right itself. I yank the blade free, plunge it deep into the right sensor, and twist the hilt with all my weight until the internal linkages snap and the construct goes limp.

Across the ditch, Hadrik finishes his target and charges the third. I pull my crossbow and loose two bolts at the remaining constructs attacking Daren's ward, drawing their fire channels away from the group.

With the pressure relieved, Daren leads Kate, Leila, and Melindra in a dead sprint for the broken gate. Hadrik tears through his fourth opponent, crushing its power housing under a heavy boot.

Heavy stomping vibrates through the valley. A dozen more iron golems from the outer patrol rings are closing in fast, their chest vents glowing as they prepare to fire.

Daren reaches the threshold and roars back across the ditch.

"Fall back to the gate!" he yells. "Disengage and move! Before the second wave locks us down!"

}
