ID: B3-Ch02a-Rubble
TEXT:

 Illuna, Hadrik, and I disengage and sprint for the broken portal. We clear the jagged gap just as the two closest golems unleash their fire beams. Daren sets his boots and raises his shield, expanding a white barrier across the archway. The twin fire streams slam into the ward, generating a concussive shockwave that showers the corridor in stone fragments. Hadrik bats the largest boulders aside with sweeping backhands.

We push past the entry arch and down the main thoroughfare. The golems halt at the shattered threshold, their internal programming barring them from firing into populated city streets.

"What comes first?" Kate asks as we pass groups of panicked citizens gathering along the market lane. "Do we seek cover, or push for the palace?"

"We maintain momentum toward the castle," Daren says, scanning the avenues. "Hesitation gives the garrison time to mobilize. Melindra, which route leads to the palace?"

"Through the Perrelion Plaza," Melindra says. "Assuming the district layout remains intact since my departure, it offers the most direct approach. Follow me."

Melindra takes the lead through the winding market lanes. More citizens spill from their doorways to gawk at the destroyed gatehouse, while hovering metallic skiffs glide calmly along the skyways above, unbothered by the chaos below.

"Leila," Daren asks as we run, "can you reach your father? Is there any way to signal our presence?"

"No," Leila writes, glowing azure letters hanging in the air beside her shoulder. "He carried no equipment during our flight from Thilias, so I have no transceiver channel. He promised he would establish contact once I reached Ollendor, but finding us will take time."

"Our arrival will not remain quiet for long," Daren assures her with a faint smile. "Once the commotion begins, he will know where to look."

"Let us hope so," Leila writes.

The surrounding architecture grows stranger with every block. Tall, cylindrical towers with curved glass facades stand alongside four-story residential spires built entirely of riveted metal, their plates dusted with a shimmering coating of seredium. No two structures share a blueprint; the entire district looks like an assortment of competing prototypes thrown together without a master plan.

choice("Continue", B3-Ch02b-Weird, v_current_scene = B3-Ch02b-Weird)
